# S14p in the world ("as the host's story", 19.24), guest g (a k10 character: k2 dies on the route's rock slope): its
# lobby plays its own story (which has flag 505); through the lobby gate it joins o's instance in stag0101 and plays o's
# story there (o's card without 505: g's engine lacks it in the field). It steps on matb01, whose hint panel sets 505: new
# to the host's story and plausible there, merged into o's keeper at once. run.py's "story_saved" times o's online_story
# row from this script's "505 set" line (ten seconds at most). On to stag0102 (a stage group of o's instance): 505 stays.
campaign until stage=stagml11
talk until control,frames>=60
log in the lobby
idle until epoch>=@100
explore mate00 yes until stage=stag0101,control
log in the field
idle until frames>=120 fail flag:505=1
log 505 not in the host's story
mat matb01 no until flag:505=1
log 505 set
talk until control,frames>=60
route {route:stag0101_west>218,-26}
mat matz02 yes until stage=stag0102,control
log in stag0102
idle until frames>=120 fail flag:505=0
log 505 kept
idle until frames>=60
